# Implement Page Up/Page Down Navigation for Menus

The goal is to allow the user to navigate between application views (Inbox, Today, Completed, All) using the `PageUp` and `PageDown` keys.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> This change adds global hotkeys `PageUp` and `PageDown`. These will be intercepted at the top level to switch the main filter (view).

## Proposed Changes

### [flowstate]

#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///C:/Users/mheyi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/flowstate/App.tsx)
- Add `PageUp` and `PageDown` to the global [handleKeyDown](file:///C:/Users/mheyi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/flowstate/App.tsx#117-211) event listener.
- `PageDown`: Switch to the next menu item (cycling).
- `PageUp`: Switch to the previous menu item (cycling).
- Ensure `sidebarIndex` state is updated to reflect the new active item.
- Ensure `filter` in `useUIStore` is updated.
- Prevent default behavior to avoid scrolling (if applicable/desired, usually `PageUp`/[Down](file:///C:/Users/mheyi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/flowstate/App.tsx#117-211) scroll, but here they change views).

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Open the application.
2. Press `PageDown`. Verify the view changes from "Inbox" to "Today".
3. Press `PageDown` again. Verify "Today" -> "Done" (Completed).
4. Press `PageDown` again. Verify "Done" -> "All".
5. Press `PageDown` again. Verify "All" -> "Inbox" (Cycle).
6. Press `PageUp`. Verify the reverse order.
7. Verify that the sidebar active indicator updates accordingly.
